# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# abid-bot
#
# In git: the pipeline itself -- bin/, the atts/ XML templates, the run
# scripts, params/params2, docs.
#
# Not in git: your simulation data, and everything setup.sh or the run scripts
# regenerate from it. All of it is per-case, most of it is enormous, and none
# of it means anything in another checkout -- overlap.txt and xml*/ in
# particular encode which h5 folders this one tree happens to hold.
#
# Note: git only honours '#' at the start of a line, so every comment here is
# on its own line. A trailing comment would become part of the pattern.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- generated by setup.sh -------------------------------------------------
# xml*/  per-frame view_/volume_/time_/spin_ files built by setmovie.py
#        and setup_spinvtk_*.py; setup.sh [N] rebuilds them wholesale.
# bhdata/  gpto3d output: horizon .gp -> .3d
# cm.txt   setup_cm.sh: centre of mass per frame
# bin/gpto3d  compiled from gpto3d.cpp by setup_bh.sh
xml*/
bhdata/
cm.txt
bin/grid_code/bhcen[0-9].txt
bin/gpto3d

# --- generated by movieSeq_v2_arg.bash, inside setup_frames ----------------
# Folder/iteration bookkeeping, rebuilt from whatever h5data/ holds at the
# time. setmovie.py walks overlap.txt to turn a frame index into a folder, so
# a stale or shared copy silently mislabels every frame.
bin/bw_many_folder_scripts/overlap.txt
bin/bw_many_folder_scripts/overlap.txt.*
bin/bw_many_folder_scripts/list_sorted.txt
bin/bw_many_folder_scripts/list_tmp.txt
bin/bw_many_folder_scripts/duplicate.txt
bin/bw_many_folder_scripts/gap.txt

# --- render output ---------------------------------------------------------
# movies/  PNG frames and stitched movies
# log/     runMulti job/run/out trees
# visitlog.py  VisIt drops this in whatever directory it runs in
movies/
log/
xml_log.txt
visitlog.py

# --- your simulation data --------------------------------------------------
# h5data/ is a symlink farm over the extracted HDF5 plus diagnostics and
# horizon files. Ignore all of it except the hand-authored geometry we ship
# and the script that rebuilds the farm.
h5data/*
!h5data/*.3d
!h5data/link_h5data.sh

# --- editing, build and crash artifacts ------------------------------------
*.orig
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]*
*~
*.rej
*.log
nohup.out
core
core.[0-9]*
*.o
a.out
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.tar.gz
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- agent / tooling scratch -----------------------------------------------
.superpowers/

# pid files written by the long-running resumable render loops (render_missing*.sh)
*.pid
